  "reason": "The operating income calculation is incorrect. Summing cost of revenue ($30,745), SG&A ($41,704), and other operating expenses ($162,287) yields $234,736 in total expenses. The reported operating income of $22,405 implies revenue of $257,141. However, using transaction data, net SG&A is −49,411 + 7,707 = −41,704, and net other operating expenses is +30,022 − 192,309 = −162,287. The correct operating income should be revenue minus these, but the statement's $22,405 does not align with the sum of the components. ASC 606-10-25-23 governs revenue recognition and expense aggregation, requiring accurate line item derivation from underlying transactions."
